nces between groups; a p-value <0.05 was considered statistically significant.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Data were weighted to account for the complex survey design and adjusted for nonresponse.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"National prevalence estimates with 95% confidence intervals and population estimates were computed\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"The number of exposure sources were summed for each student\"}], \"confidence\": \"high\", \"uncertain_fields\": [\"analytic_depth\", \"outcome_types\"]}", "type": "text"}]}